# Fixed defect 2450, 2026-11-10, lane b30-pkg: a `use` written as an
# address whose module part is a keyword, `github.com/acme/json/match`.
#
# SYMPTOM: `use_holds_an_address`, told to write `use <json>/match`, with a
# repair writing `<json>/match`: a line the parser refuses at `match`, the
# class of defect 2432's entry names.
#
# CAUSE: the module after an address was offered whatever its parts were,
# where its entry was already held to the rule a `use` path is read by.
#
# FIX: a module part that is a keyword or a word the lexer refuses leaves
# the stand-in, `parse`, and no repair, bare, quoted or nested; a module a
# `use` can write is still offered, as the last line's is.
use github.com/acme/json/match  #~ use_holds_an_address
use "github.com/acme/toml/match"  #~ use_holds_an_address
use github.com/acme/xml/text/match  #~ use_holds_an_address
use github.com/acme/csv/let  #~ use_holds_an_address
use github.com/acme/ini/parse  #~ use_holds_an_address

function main()
    print(1)
